      <activity id="e94bfe76-097d-572b-b5dc-ad49ce96e7f5" activityNameId="579d92e7-5891-5c98-b63b-6895d31755ff" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, low pressure, at consumer</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, low pressure, at consumer
Infrastructure requirements are based on estimated standard capacity. The net calorific value of natural gas is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=7262b28b-283a-3b51-a7bd-57919198ed0b
This dataset describes the energy requirements and the emissions of the low pressure distribution network.
Location: Energy requirements and emissions are based on Swiss data
Technology: The quantity of gas delivered in the low pressure network is estimated. Residential and half of commercial and of others are assumed to consume low pressure gas.
Time period: Energy requirements are from 2019 and leakage data are from 2018.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7262b28b-283a-3b51-a7bd-57919198ed0b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
